kernora-archive (1.3) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Debian's trixie-backports archive, for a newer kernel, graphics firmware
    and Mesa. Recent graphics cards, such as AMD Radeon RX 9000 and Intel Arc
    B-series, need a newer kernel and Mesa than Debian 13 ships. Only the
    kernel, firmware, Mesa, libdrm and NVIDIA's Debian driver are taken from
    it (kernora-backports.pref); everything else stays on Debian 13.
  * Updates from trixie-backports install automatically each day, like
    security updates, so the kernel keeps getting its security fixes.

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0000
kernora-archive (1.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Demo updates: an opt-in second channel, ember-demo, that gets new
    Kernora packages before everyone else. Settings > System turns it on
    and off through /usr/libexec/kernora-update-channel; turning it off
    keeps the demo versions until a normal update replaces them.

